    "trap_category": "Scope",
    "setup": "Normal market. A bank holds 25m shares quoted 90.8 / 92.4 (USD) and 35m ounces of a commodity quoted 24.0 / 26.2 (USD). Liquidation cost of a leg is half the dollar spread times the quantity.",
    "ask": "Which leg is more expensive to liquidate?",
    "options": [
      {
        "label": "The shares, because that position is far larger in dollar value",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Ranked legs by position value. Cost depends on the spread relative to price: shares 1.7%, commodity 8.8%."
      },
      {
        "label": "The commodity",
        "correct": true
      },
      {
        "label": "They cost about the same",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Treated both as 'a spread of about USD 2 on tens of millions of units' without comparing the two spreads: 1.6 versus 2.2, on different quantities."
      }
    ],
    "working": [
      {
        "label": "Shares",
        "display": "$\\tfrac12 \\times 1.6 \\times 25\\text{m} = 20.0\\text{m}$",
        "value": 20.0
      },
      {
        "label": "Commodity",
        "display": "$\\tfrac12 \\times 2.2 \\times 35\\text{m} = 38.5\\text{m}$",
        "value": 38.5
      }
    ],
    "takeaway": "A thin position in a wide-spread asset can cost more to unwind than a big position in a tight one.",
    "check": {
      "inputs": {
        "q1": 25,
        "b1": 90.8,
        "o1": 92.4,
        "q2": 35,
        "b2": 24.0,
        "o2": 26.2
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "name": "c1",
          "expr": "0.5*(o1-b1)*q1",
          "value": 20.0
        },
        {
          "name": "c2",
          "expr": "0.5*(o2-b2)*q2",
          "value": 38.5
        },
        {
          "name": "diff",
          "expr": "c2-c1",
          "value": 18.5
        },
        {
          "name": "s1",
          "expr": "(o1-b1)/((o1+b1)/2)",
          "value": 0.0174672
        },
        {
          "name": "s2",
          "expr": "(o2-b2)/((o2+b2)/2)",
          "value": 0.0876494
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "SC-bank-LRq01-04",
    "mode": "direction",
    "area": "LTR",
    "reading": "LTR-1: Liquidity Risk",
    "reading_id": "LTR-1",
    "source": {
      "kind": "bank",
      "questionId": "LR-QB-0019"
    },
    "trap_category": "Sign",
    "setup": "Stressed-market unwind, 95% ($z = 1.645$). Two long positions with perfectly correlated, normal proportional spreads: \\$25,000 with mean = sd = 0.050, and \\$40,000 with mean = sd = 0.030. Cost $= \\tfrac12 \\sum \\alpha_i(\\mu_i + z\\sigma_i)$.",
    "ask": "Compared with the normal-market unwind cost (spread means only), the stressed cost is:",
    "options": [
      {
        "label": "More than double",
        "correct": true
      },
      {
        "label": "Exactly double",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Used $\\mu + \\sigma$ and left out the z-score. With $\\sigma = \\mu$ that would double the cost, but $z = 1.645$ makes the factor $1 + 1.645$."
      },
      {
        "label": "Less than double",
        "correct": false,
        "why": "Treated the volatility term as a small cushion on top of the mean. Here $\\sigma$ equals $\\mu$, so $z\\sigma$ alone is 1.645 times the mean."
      }
    ],
    "working": [
      {
        "label": "Normal cost",
        "display": "$\\tfrac12(25{,}000 \\times 0.050 + 40{,}000 \\times 0.030) = 1{,}225$",
        "value": 1225
      },
      {
        "label": "Stressed factor",
        "display": "$\\mu + z\\sigma = \\mu(1 + 1.645) = 2.645\\mu$",
        "value": 2.645
      },
      {
        "label": "Stressed cost",
        "display": "$1{,}225 \\times 2.645 \\approx 3{,}240$",
        "value": 3240
      }
    ],
    "takeaway": "When the spread's sd equals its mean, the stressed cost is $(1+z)$ times the normal cost.",
    "check": {
      "inputs": {
        "a1": 25000,
        "m1": 0.05,
        "a2": 40000,
        "m2": 0.03,
        "z": 1.645
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "name": "normal",
          "expr": "0.5*(a1*m1+a2*m2)",
          "value": 1225.0
        },
        {
          "name": "stressed",
          "expr": "0.5*(a1*(m1+z*m1)+a2*(m2+z*m2))",
          "value": 3240.12
        },
        {
          "name": "ratio",
          "expr": "stressed/normal",
          "value": 2.645
        },
        {
          "name": "slip_no_z",
          "expr": "0.5*(a1*(m1+m1)+a2*(m2+m2))/normal",
          "value": 2.0
        }
      ]
    }
  },
